| **Evidence used** | state-level panel data and homelessness rates as well as labor market data, entrepreneurship measures |
| **Methods** | **Dynamic econometric methods**, including **Panel Vector Autoregression (PVAR), Granger causality testing, and Cholesky forecast-error variance decomposition.** |
| **Underlying Assumption** | ??? |
| **Main insight** | **Higher levels of entrepreneurial activity and labor market freedom may reduce homelessness by expanding economic opportunity and reducing barriers to employment.** |
