| **Questions asked** | How do economic conditions influence housing insecurity? | ? |
| **Evidence used** | State-level economic indicators, labor market data, entrepreneurship measures, homelessness rates | ? |
| **Methods** | Econometric analysis of state-level panel data | ? |
| **Underlying Assumption** | Economic systems, incentives, and institutional conditions influence human behavior and social outcomes. | ? |
| **Main insight** | **Higher levels of entrepreneurial activity and labor market freedom may reduce homelessness by expanding economic opportunity and reducing barriers to employment.** | **Public policy design, particularly access to direct cash assistance, can play an important role in reducing family homelessness.** |
]]></Markdown>
